- **The start at {{e1.started_hhmm_utc}} is not a measurement.** The AI wrote nothing, so the score of {{e1.r1}} says nothing about a language or a model; it shows a fault of the runner. The {{e1.agent_seconds_counted}} seconds in its record are not time the AI worked but the time that passed until the command failed.
- **The start at {{e2.started_hhmm_utc}} is a complete run, and it is not counted.** It was made with the runner as it was before the token was taken off the command line and before the process table was watched. After the runner was changed, Python was run again, and to keep to one run per language only the run with the changed runner is counted. Its numbers (AI working time {{e2.agent_seconds_counted}} seconds, {{e2.wall_seconds}} seconds in all, {{e2.turns}} turns) are close to those of the counted Python run ({{run.python.asum}} seconds, {{run.python.wall}} seconds, {{run.python.turns}} turns). So Python ran to the end twice that day, and "once per language" in this document means the counted runs.

