### The two effects apart

At the plan's capacity, the chance that the baseline measurement ends by {{row_end_long}} moves like this.

- Inputs before the pilot: {{planning.before.p_baseline_by_row_end}}%.
- Only finished work counted as finished: {{planning.finished_only.p_baseline_by_row_end}}%. By itself this effect hardly moves the chance. Entering finished work as finished on {{date_short}} makes what follows it start the next day with all its work ahead, so the middle date for the measuring tool being complete even moves later, from {{planning.before.b_runner.p50}} to {{planning.finished_only.b_runner.p50}}.
- Only the pilot's numbers entered: {{planning.numbers_only.p_baseline_by_row_end}}%. Nearly all of the rise comes from this effect.
- Both: {{planning.after_x1.p_baseline_by_row_end}}%.

The chance of reaching the direction-fixing gate by {{gate_long}} is {{planning.before.p_gate_by_its_date}}%, {{planning.finished_only.p_gate_by_its_date}}%, {{planning.numbers_only.p_gate_by_its_date}}% and {{planning.after_x1.p_gate_by_its_date}}% in the same order.

Under today's conditions (one shared Claude account, counted as about {{claude_shared.days_a_week}} working days a week) the chance for the baseline measurement is, in the same order, {{claude_shared.before.p_baseline_by_row_end}}%, {{claude_shared.finished_only.p_baseline_by_row_end}}%, {{claude_shared.numbers_only.p_baseline_by_row_end}}%, {{claude_shared.after_x1.p_baseline_by_row_end}}%, and the chance for the gate {{claude_shared.before.p_gate_by_its_date}}%, {{claude_shared.finished_only.p_gate_by_its_date}}%, {{claude_shared.numbers_only.p_gate_by_its_date}}%, {{claude_shared.after_x1.p_gate_by_its_date}}%. With one account used for Dodam alone (counted as about {{claude_dedicated.days_a_week}} working days a week) it is {{claude_dedicated.before.p_baseline_by_row_end}}%, {{claude_dedicated.finished_only.p_baseline_by_row_end}}%, {{claude_dedicated.numbers_only.p_baseline_by_row_end}}%, {{claude_dedicated.after_x1.p_baseline_by_row_end}}% for the baseline measurement and {{claude_dedicated.before.p_gate_by_its_date}}%, {{claude_dedicated.finished_only.p_gate_by_its_date}}%, {{claude_dedicated.numbers_only.p_gate_by_its_date}}%, {{claude_dedicated.after_x1.p_gate_by_its_date}}% for the gate. In these two cases the rise is a few percentage points only, which cannot be told from the difference between seeds (up to {{noise.chances_move_up_to_points}} percentage points).

### The verdict

- **The pilot**: finished on {{date_long}}. Its mark of being done, "we know what percent of the subscription limit one run uses", is half met. Time and tokens are measured; for the limits only an upper bound is known.
- **What happens to the dates (the decision)**: the dates of the schedule stay as the plan's dates at the plan's capacity, and are labelled so. The figures for today's conditions are given beside them. Whether the dates move is judged after what one account gives in a week has been measured. The reason: the two numbers that move the dates (what a week gives, and how long a larger model works) have not been measured yet. Dates are moved neither earlier nor later on an assumption that has not been measured.
- **The baseline measurement ({{row_start_long}} to {{row_end_long}})**: at the plan's capacity (about {{planning.days_a_week}} working days a week) the chance of ending by {{row_end_long}} is {{planning.after_x1.p_baseline_by_row_end}}% as measured, {{planning.after_x2.p_baseline_by_row_end}}% if the AI working time is {{x2.factor}} times and {{planning.after_x4.p_baseline_by_row_end}}% if it is {{x4.factor}} times (it was {{planning.before.p_baseline_by_row_end}}% with the inputs before the pilot); as measured the middle date is {{planning.after_x1.b_baseline.p50}} and the {{pct80}}% date {{planning.after_x1.b_baseline.p80}}. Under today's conditions (one shared account, counted as about {{claude_shared.days_a_week}} working days a week) it is, as measured, a chance of {{claude_shared.after_x1.p_baseline_by_row_end}}%, middle {{claude_shared.after_x1.b_baseline.p50}}, {{pct80}}% {{claude_shared.after_x1.b_baseline.p80}}. With one account used for Dodam alone (counted as about {{claude_dedicated.days_a_week}} working days a week) it is a chance of {{claude_dedicated.after_x1.p_baseline_by_row_end}}%, middle {{claude_dedicated.after_x1.b_baseline.p50}}, {{pct80}}% {{claude_dedicated.after_x1.b_baseline.p80}}.
- **The direction-fixing gate ({{gate_long}})**: at the plan's capacity the chance of reaching it by that day is {{planning.after_x1.p_gate_by_its_date}}% as measured, {{planning.after_x2.p_gate_by_its_date}}% at {{x2.factor}} times and {{planning.after_x4.p_gate_by_its_date}}% at {{x4.factor}} times (it was {{planning.before.p_gate_by_its_date}}% with the inputs before the pilot); as measured the middle date is {{planning.after_x1.g_dir.p50}} and the {{pct80}}% date {{planning.after_x1.g_dir.p80}}. Under today's conditions it is, as measured, a chance of {{claude_shared.after_x1.p_gate_by_its_date}}%, middle {{claude_shared.after_x1.g_dir.p50}}, {{pct80}}% {{claude_shared.after_x1.g_dir.p80}}. With one account used for Dodam alone it is a chance of {{claude_dedicated.after_x1.p_gate_by_its_date}}%, middle {{claude_dedicated.after_x1.g_dir.p50}}, {{pct80}}% {{claude_dedicated.after_x1.g_dir.p80}}.
- **How to read these figures**: the figures for today's conditions say there is little chance of keeping the plan's dates. But the assumption they stand on (one account gives about {{claude_shared.days_a_week}} to {{claude_dedicated.days_a_week}} working days a week) has never been measured. The pilot itself was finished with one Claude account {{pilot_days_early}} days earlier than planned. So measuring that assumption comes first.
- **The time freed by finishing early**: {{pilot_days_before_end}} days remain until the day the pilot was to end. They go to the two pieces of work that decide when the baseline measurement starts (the {{plan.tasks}} tasks and completing the measuring tool) and to the measurements described above.
